, and non-disease premodifiers, along with a scope note tying it back to the existing Modifier definition.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Principle: Disease Span as Leftmost Premodifier of a Molecular-Entity Head**\n  - **IF** a disease-denoting span (a full disease name or its acronym) occupies the leftmost premodifier slot of a noun phrase whose nominal head denotes a molecular entity (a gene, protein, or similar nomenclature-bearing noun, including forms with numeric or designator suffixes), **THEN** label the disease span as `Modifier`. The molecular status of the head does not license an `O` label for the disease span.\n  - **Negative constraint (does NOT apply):**\n    - When the disease-denoting span is the phrase head itself, or appears inside a postmodifying prepositional phrase (e.g., a \"gene for [disease]\" relation), since neither is a premodifier position.\n    - When the candidate string is a gene or protein symbol that carries no disease reading in context, so there is no disease span to tag.\n    - When the leftmost premodifier is a non-disease term (e.g., anatomical, chemical, or organism terms), since the rule concerns only disease premodifiers.\n  - **Scope:** This rule governs only the label of the disease span. It does not authorize labeling the molecular-entity head or the full identifier as `SpecificDisease` or `DiseaseClass`, and it does not alter `CompositeMention` boundaries. It is consistent with the `Modifier` definition, in which a disease term functions adjectivally within a larger noun phrase.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2011, "output_tokens": 3097, "output_tokens_details": {"